# The specification lives in one place: the standard's repository, published
# here as /spec/. A markdown copy used to sit beside it, unlinked and two
# versions behind — nothing referenced it, but it answered 200, so anyone who
# found it through a search engine was reading IAES 1.2 without knowing.
#
# It is gone. The URL still resolves, to the page that is actually maintained.
/spec/IAES_SPEC.md    /spec/    301

# Every published event schema references its envelope as "iaes-envelope.schema.json", the file name in the
# standard's repository. Against an $id of https://iaes.dev/schema/<major>/<type> that resolves to
# /schema/<major>/iaes-envelope.schema.json, which answered 404: a validator fetching the schemas from this site
# could not resolve the envelope (the SDKs never noticed, because they validate against copies they ship).
# Served here as a 200 rewrite of the envelope's canonical path, so no schema's bytes change.
/schema/v1/iaes-envelope.schema.json    /schema/v1/envelope    200
/schema/v2/iaes-envelope.schema.json    /schema/v2/envelope    200
